      {
        "id": 236583,
        "name": "Jeysie",
        "username": "Jeysie",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-04T14:24:27.281Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"JoeSteeloak\" data-post=\"471\" data-topic=\"6706\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/joesteeloak/48/4853_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> JoeSteeloak:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can’t seem to find the different comic covers easily through the wiki. How would I go about doing that?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Two places.</p>\n<p>One, the main category which I reformatted into an actual nice gallery: <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Category:Comic_Covers\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Category:Comic Covers - Sentinel Comics Wiki</a><br>\nTwo, I recently added a tab with just the Writers’ Room covers specifically to the Podcasts page itself: <a href=\"https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Podcasts\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Podcasts - Sentinel Comics Wiki</a></p>\n<p>I think at some point I want to make it so when you hover over the listings on the Podcasts index you get some relevant context for that episode that shows in a pop-up including things like the covers, but this at least adds the covers <em>somehow</em> which I probably should have done way before now.</p>",
