        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-04-06T17:34:18.519Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"JoeSteeloak\" data-post=\"477\" data-topic=\"6706\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/joesteeloak/48/4853_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> JoeSteeloak:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If you search the wiki for <em>Comic Covers</em> it does not show up</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It’s because I repurposed a category page rather than making a page proper. Only things in the “Main” namespace show up in the wiki search, things like the Category namespace do not.</p>\n<p>One of the (many) reasons the wiki structure could use an overhaul is to find better homes for these sorts of things. It’s one of the things I added to the Sidebar for now, though.</p>",
